 ## V5 S1 trail scale update
 
 At the user's selection, the existing S1 trail atlas was downscaled to approximately 65% (uniform factor 354/543 = 118/181 = 0.651934, rounded to integer pixel dimensions); six frame crops are 59x118 instead of 90.5x181. Frame timing and VFX binding are unchanged. This modifies the supplied raster asset without regenerating it. It has not been calibrated in a TFM2 match.
+
+
+## V6 follow-up — movement, S2 diagnostics, target impact VFX
+
+V6 shortens the S2 `CasterAnimation("skill2")` from 180 ticks to 12. The native 180-tick cyclone buff, 14 hit pulses, 36,000 radius, movement buff and damage/shred code are unchanged. The new DLL writes watched-live-match `[BALMOND_S2]` start/passive/pulse target-count diagnostics to the existing `mlbb_heroes.log`.
+
+The Ultimate still uses Balmond's prior directional `DirDot` damage fan and native execute. The caster-bound slash trigger is replaced by a target-position `ViewEffect` nested in the fan's per-target effects; its binding follows the struck target for the brief hit. The existing one-frame slash is resized to 161x98 (80% of v5's 201x122); timing is unchanged. This adapts BoDUD Miss Fortune's separation of fan hit selection and target hit visual; it does not copy her 40-degree gameplay cone or 12-wave channel.
+
+V6's Rust unit tests (75) and Windows x86-64 build passed, and the v6/package static audits passed. No TFM2 match test was performed, so the S2 movement/damage and target-following VFX remain to be checked in game.
